  "objectives": [
    "Determine steric number from a Lewis structure by counting bonding and lone-pair electron domains around a central atom.",
    "Predict electron-domain geometry from steric number using the five fundamental VSEPR arrangements.",
    "Distinguish electron-domain geometry from molecular geometry when lone pairs are present.",
    "Explain why lone pairs occupy more angular space than bonding pairs and how this changes bond angles from ideal values.",
    "Apply VSEPR theory to real molecules including H2O, NH3, CH4, PF5, SF6, and XeF4."
