      "institution": "MTSU",
      "dateCreated": "2026-07-07",
      "educationalObjectives": [
        "Count bonding pairs and lone pairs around a central atom to determine steric number.",
        "Describe VSEPR as a model of minimizing electron-pair repulsion in three dimensions.",
        "Relate a 2D Lewis structure to a 3D arrangement problem."
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "Look at the central atom and count each bonding region and lone pair as one electron domain.",
        "Use the Next and Previous buttons to compare the flat Lewis picture with the 3D VSEPR model.",
        "Notice that molecular shape depends on where bonded atoms are, while electron-domain geometry includes lone pairs too."
